UPDATE places SET description_en='The Kempton Steam Museum is home to the Kempton Park steam engines which are two large triple-expansion steam engines, dating from 1926–1929, at the Kempton Park Waterworks in south-west London. They were ordered by the Metropolitan Water Board and manufactured by Worthington-Simpson in Newark-on-Trent.', description_it='Il Kempton Steam Museum ospita i motori a vapore Kempton Park, due grandi motori a vapore a tripla espansione, risalenti al 1926-1929, presso il Kempton Park Waterworks di Londra sud-ovest. Furono ordinati dal Metropolitan Water Board e fabbricati da Worthington-Simpson a Newark-on-Trent.',
